{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is not met, so the 5.00 SGD fee must be voided. POL-NS-23 requires BOTH at least one in-app chat message sent by the driver AND at least one in-app call placed by the driver, both before trip_record.cancelled_at (16:13:40). The trip record's derived contact_before_cancel block reports message_count 0 and obligation_met false: the two in-app calls at 16:09:30 and 16:11:50 satisfy the call limb, but the message limb has nothing behind it. Where either limb is missing the fee is voided and the rider is not charged, with no driver compensation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05070", "EV-CHAT-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The single driver message in the chat log was sent AFTER the cancellation. MSG-05070-002 from sender DRIVER was sent at 16:13:55 and delivered at 16:13:58 - fifteen seconds after the trip was cancelled at 16:13:40 - and it reads 'I cancel already, you never come down'. A message sent after cancelled_at cannot satisfy POL-NS-23, and the driver's own words establish that the cancellation decision came before he messaged the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05070", "EV-TRIP-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's answer that he 'also sent message' is not supported by the record. The only message preceding his own is MSG-05070-001 at 16:07:28, whose sender is SYSTEM ('Your driver has arrived.'), an automated platform notification, not an in-app chat message sent by the driver as POL-NS-23 requires. The driver's assertion of the message limb is therefore contradicted by the two complete artifacts that carry the fact, and the caveat in the rider's own account - that no message was sent saying where the driver was - is borne out.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05070", "EV-TRIP-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages.sender",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Remedy follows directly. The rider is the filing party, the fare ledger shows payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00 and a 5.00 SGD cancellation fee applied at 16:13:44, so the whole contested amount is still with the platform. POL-NS-23's remedy is FULL_REFUND of the fee charged, with no driver compensation, and under POL-GEN-03 FULL_REFUND means the filing party is entirely right and the whole contested amount is returned. The refund is 5.00 SGD; driver_compensation_sgd is 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05070", "EV-TRIP-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The contact obligation does not depend on the free wait, so the fee fails even on the driver's best reading of the clock. Even assuming the driver did arrive at the pickup (the GPS arrival check corroborates the 16:07:25 arrival event, nearest fix 2.16 m inside the 50 m STANDARD radius) and the 300 s free wait under POL-NS-21 ran from that arrival to expiry at 16:12:25 before the 16:13:40 cancellation, POL-NS-23 imposes an independent condition that had to be satisfied before cancelling. It was not, and POL-NS-23 provides no room to cure the omission after the fact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05070", "EV-GPS-05070", "EV-CHAT-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation is warranted. Every fact POL-NS-23 needs - whether the driver messaged and called before cancelling - is carried by artifacts that are COMPLETE at weight 1.0 (the chat log and the trip record), so POL-GEN-26's 'fact the record cannot establish' route does not open and nothing is held. The one absent artifact on the case, EV-ADVIS-05070-01, is a TRAFFIC_ADVISORY with admissibility status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0; it carries no fact about driver contact and is cited only to record its absence under POL-GEN-02.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05070", "EV-TRIP-05070", "EV-ADVIS-05070-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The AI can and should decide this case finally. The disputed value is 5.00 SGD (the cancellation fee on the ledger), below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence; neither profile carries a fraud flag (rider 0, driver 0), so the 0.95 confidence bar never engages; and POL-NS-26 fixes the no-show fee at 5.00 SGD. A FULL_REFUND of 5.00 SGD is therefore a ruling this tribunal is competent to issue on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05070", "EV-RPROF-05070", "EV-DPROF-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "relies_on": "authority.value_band",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider did not abandon the pickup. The chat log shows the rider replying 'What? I was coming down now' at 16:14:30, fifty seconds after the driver cancelled, and the message was read at 16:14:55: the rider was at the device and on the way down. The driver's characterisation 'you never come down' is his own gloss on a rider who responded almost immediately once he was told the trip was gone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-no-show referral arises. POL-NS-25 operates on rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d and only when that counter is present; the rider profile snapshot at filing does not carry that field at all, so the counter cannot be taken to 3 by adding this trip and no review flag under POL-NS-25 follows from this dispute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05070"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-25"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
